                <pb facs="0438" n="294" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg294"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/221: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-20T10:00:00+08:00">August 20, 1929—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 20—7:04 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>737. My 730, August 18, 6 [<hi rendition="#italic">4</hi>] p.m. Following from
                    American Consul at Harbin: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“August 19, 4 p.m. Customs reports from Taheiho state Chinese military
                            are about to evacuate from that place and that raiding parties,
                            presumably Soviet, are crossing the Amur and pillaging on Chinese
                            side.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
